Observations:
Parent total time is roughly constant around 1–2 ms, showing the main overhead comes from process creation (fork() and pipe() setup).

As N increases, child computation times scale linearly — but remain small because summation is simple and CPU caching helps.

The children finish faster than total parent time, because the parent also waits (wait()) and synchronizes with both pipes.

